        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. French court refuses trial on use of toxic insecticide in French West Indies Health Issued on: 22/06/2026 - 17:43 Modified: 22/06/2026 - 17:48 A French court has ruled against a trial on the use of a known toxic insecticide in the French West Indies, shutting down the possibility of an investigation in a health scandal that has been ongoing for 20 years. Despite being labelled as possibly carcinogenic in 1979, chlordécone was used between 1972 until 1993 - thanks to a by-law that allowed it to circumvent its ban, introduced in 1990. FRANCE 24's Shirli Sitbon tells us more. Ebola : Healthworkers in DR Congo worry for their life amid deadly outbreak 20/06/2026 Africa Pancreatic cancer: Dr. Pudlarz praises 'new generation targeted therapy' that inhibits gene mutation 02/06/2026 Health Race to contain ebola outbreak in war-torn DRC where weak infrastructure hampers response 20/05/2026 Africa Funding and Ebola epidemic loom over WHO's annual summit 19/05/2026 Health DRC Ebola outbreak 'way bigger than what we see now', virologist says 18/05/2026 Health ‘High time to push peace agenda’: Ebola outbreak in DRC spreads in conflict-hit, hard-to-reach areas 18/05/2026 Africa WHO declares emergency as Ebola outbreak kills more than 80 in DR Congo 17/05/2026 Africa Why are cruise ships such fertile ground for infection? 14/05/2026 Health Hantavirus close contacts in France have so far tested negative 14/05/2026 Health"
