        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. US hails 'good progress' with Iran after first round of talks concludes Middle East Issued on: 22/06/2026 - 17:20 US Vice President JD Vance has said that a first round of US-Iran talks in Switzerland had laid a good foundation for reaching a final deal on ending the Middle East war that the US and Israel began in February. Vance's comments came after he met with Iran's parliamentary speaker Mohammad Bagher Qalibaf on June 21 and 22. The mediation effort in Switzerland had rocky moments, but the talks also led to some agreements between the two sides. For Iraqi minorities, World Cup representation is a source of pride 22/06/2026 Middle East 'JD Vance put lipstick on a pig: Iranians have the upper hand ' in peace negotiations 22/06/2026 Middle East What do Iranians think of the Iran-US deal? 22/06/2026 Middle East Replay: JD Vance addresses US-Iran talks 22/06/2026 Middle East US-Iran's first round of talks concludes despite Trump threatening strikes 22/06/2026 Middle East US-Iran talks 'off to strained, asymetric start' as Tehran hails success 22/06/2026 Middle East Trump threatens to strike Iran over support for Hezbollah as fighting continues in Lebanon 21/06/2026 Middle East Israeli strikes start again in Lebanon after several-hour lull, amid US-Iran talks 21/06/2026 Middle East Sailors trapped in Hormuz strait, dodging drones and rationing food 21/06/2026 Middle East"
